  <h3>What is the difference between Cold Brew and Cold Brewed Coffee?</h3>
  <p>We, at Bona Fide, have been frequently asked what is the difference between these two methods, here is the answer.</p>
  <p>Cold brew coffee started out as a term for coffee made with cold water only. However, it evolved into a loose term that refers to cold coffee methods in general.</p>
  <p>Cold-brewed coffee is only brewed with cold water and needs to be refrigerated the entire time it is held. It generally has a short shelf life and goes sour quickly due to microbiological contamination in the handling process. Our proprietary process is called Craft Draft because it is not a traditional cold-brewed process. It can be called a cold brew coffee, but not cold-brewed, because we do use a hot step in the method.</p>
